 real automatic renewals (serial rotated at 11:57:00 and again at 11:59:00, confirmed against cert-renew.log). Then performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured a healthy baseline (boot_id, services, cert, HTTPS 200), issued a native `reboot`, confirmed the node dropped and later returned with a different boot_id, and verified nginx, crond, the crontab entry, the persisted cert, and HTTPS on 8443 all recovered post-restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed nginx and openssl on node1 (Alpine 3.23)\",\"Wrote /usr/local/bin/renew-cert.sh: generates a 5-minute-validity self-signed cert via openssl req -x509 -not_after, renews when remaining validity < 180s, then runs nginx -t and nginx -s reload\",\"Configured nginx server block listening on 8443 ssl using /etc/nginx/ssl/{cert,key}.pem\",\"Enabled nginx and crond in the default OpenRC runlevel, and installed a '* * * * *' crontab entry running the renewal script every minute\",\"Generated the initial certificate and started nginx; verified HTTPS 200 on port 8443\",\"Ran a continuous live probe (curl + cert serial every 2s) spanning two real automatic cron-triggered renewals, observing zero downtime across each cert rotation\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, service status, cert state, HTTPS response)\",\"Issued a native reboot on node1, polled until exec access returned, and confirmed boot_id changed\",\"Verified post-restart recovery: nginx and crond auto-started, crontab persisted, cert file persisted and still valid, HTTPS 200 still served, and re-ran the renewal script to confirm the mechanism is intact\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"HTTPS served on port 8443 with a valid certificate\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7241b4d3245b4130\",\"cmd-d90eab938dfc4eb8\"],\"summary\":\"curl -sk https://$NODE_IP:8443/ returns HTTP 200; openssl x509 shows a valid, non-expired cert bound to nginx's ssl_certificate config\"},{\"requirement\":\"Certificate renews automatically before expiry\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-bc7cd978914e47bb\",\"cmd-6d3fcbadac78450c\"],\"summary\":\"Live probe log shows cert serial changing (1790683020->1790683140) exactly at cron tick 11:59:00 while cert-renew.log records unattended cron-triggered renewals at 11:54:36, 11:57:00, and 11:59:00, each renewing ~3 minutes before the prior cert's expiry\"},{\"requirement\":\"Service picks up each new cert while continuing to answer requests (no downtime)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-bc7cd978914e47bb\"],\"summary\":\"Continuous 2-second curl polling shows unbroken HTTP 200 responses across the exact second the cert serial rotated (11:59:01), proving nginx's graceful `nginx -s reload` picked up the new cert without dropping traffic\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline captured\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d90eab938dfc4eb8\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 2057e0f8-1008-4a72-a9e4-eee4fda2620f, nginx/crond both 'started', valid cert, HTTP 200, and persisted crontab entry before reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restarted via native mechanism, ack returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-531410e5ad1d44b7\",\"cmd-f7f942861a2a4aa2\"],\"summary\":\"Issued backgrounded `reboot` which acknowledged and returned immediately; the very next poll got connection reset, confirming the node went down\"},{\"requirement\":\"Boot identity changed after restart (proof of actual reboot, not just service restart)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-80c6c27bd96545eb\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id is 9a2a2188-0ff3-4752-a4af-94cd04011717, different from the pre-restart baseline 2057e0f8-1008-4a72-a9e4-eee4fda2620f\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of required services, data, and renewal mechanism\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6c1b31252a0d4e73\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot: nginx and crond auto-started (enabled at boot), the persisted cert/key and crontab entry survived, HTTPS on 8443 returned HTTP 200 again, and manually invoking renew-cert.sh confirmed the renewal logic still functions correctly (no-op since cert not yet near expiry)\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Set up HTTPS on node1:8443 via nginx with a self-signed cert that auto-renews via a busybox-crond minute-tick script (renew-cert.sh), which regenerates the cert 3 minutes before its 5-minute expiry and gracefully reloads nginx (`nginx -s reload`) so it picks up the new cert with zero dropped requests. Verified this live: a continuous curl probe showed unbroken HTTP 200s across two real automatic renewals (serial rotated at 11:57:00 and again at 11:59:00, confirmed against cert-renew.log). Then performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured a healthy baseline (boot_id, services, cert, HTTPS 200), issued a native `reboot`, confirmed the node dropped and later returned with a different boot_id, and verified nginx, crond, the crontab entry, the persisted cert, and HTTPS on 8443 all recovered post-restart.","actions_performed":["Installed nginx and openssl on node1 (Alpine 3.23)","Wrote /usr/local/bin/renew-cert.sh: generates a 5-minute-validity self-signed cert via openssl req -x509 -not_after, renews when remaining validity < 180s, then runs nginx -t and nginx -s reload","Configured nginx server block listening on 8443 ssl using /etc/nginx/ssl/{cert,key}.pem","Enabled nginx and crond in the default OpenRC runlevel, and installed a '* * * * *' crontab entry running the renewal script every minute","Generated the initial certificate and started nginx; verified HTTPS 200 on port 8443","Ran a continuous live probe (curl + cert serial every 2s) spanning two real automatic cron-triggered renewals, observing zero downtime across each cert rotation","Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, service status, cert state, HTTPS response)","Issued a native reboot on node1, polled until exec access returned, and confirmed boot_id changed","Verified post-restart recovery: nginx and crond auto-started, crontab persisted, cert file persisted and still valid, HTTPS 200 still served, and re-ran the renewal script to confirm the mechanism is intact"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"HTTPS served on port 8443 with a valid certificate","command_ids":["cmd-7241b4d3245b4130","cmd-d90eab938dfc4eb8"],"summary":"curl -sk https://$NODE_IP:8443/ returns HTTP 200; openssl x509 shows a valid, non-expired cert bound to nginx's ssl_certificate config"},{"requirement":"Certificate renews automatically before expiry","command_ids":["cmd-bc7cd978914e47bb","cmd-6d3fcbadac78450c"],"summary":"Live probe log shows cert serial changing (1790683020->1790683140) exactly at cron tick 11:59:00 while cert-renew.log records unattended cron-triggered renewals at 11:54:36, 11:57:00, and 11:59:00, each renewing ~3 minutes before the prior cert's expiry"},{"requirement":"Service picks up each new cert while continuing to answer requests (no downtime)","command_ids":["cmd-bc7cd978914e47bb"],"summary":"Continuous 2-second curl polling shows unbroken HTTP 200 responses across the exact second the cert serial rotated (11:59:01), proving nginx's graceful `nginx -s reload` picked up the new cert without dropping traffic"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline captured","command_ids":["cmd-d90eab938dfc4eb8"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 2057e0f8-1008-4a72-a9e4-eee4fda2620f, nginx/crond both 'started', valid cert, HTTP 200, and persisted crontab entry before reboot"},{"requirement":"Node restarted via native mechanism, ack returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-531410e5ad1d44b7","cmd-f7f942861a2a4aa2"],"summary":"Issued backgrounded `reboot` which acknowledged and returned immediately; the very next poll got connection reset, confirming the node went down"},{"requirement":"Boot identity changed after restart (proof of actual reboot, not just service restart)","command_ids":["cmd-80c6c27bd96545eb"],"summary":"Post-restart /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id is 9a2a2188-0ff3-4752-a4af-94cd04011717, different from the pre-restart baseline 2057e0f8-1008-4a72-a9e4-eee4fda2620f"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of required services, data, and renewal mechanism","command_ids":["cmd-6c1b31252a0d4e73"],"summary":"After reboot: nginx and crond auto-started (enabled at boot), the persisted cert/key and crontab entry survived, HTTPS on 8443 returned HTTP 200 again, and manually invoking renew-cert.sh confirmed the renewal logic still functions correctly (no-op since cert not yet near expiry)"}]},"ttft_ms":8121,"type":"result","duration_ms":458472,"uuid":"48b4b3dd-1c20-4689-819c-26279d371324","ttft_stream_ms":704,"time_to_request_ms":75,"first_content_frame_ms":704,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
